{"results":[{"id":"69b18f0dc8f031c3594cfcc9","name":"RondoDox Botnet: From Zero to 174 Exploited Vulnerabilities","description":"The RondoDox botnet has emerged as a significant threat, exploiting 174 different vulnerabilities since May 2025. It primarily targets IoT devices and internet-exposed services for DoS attacks. The botnet's infrastructure includes exploiting and hosting components, with evidence suggesting the use of compromised residential IPs. RondoDox's operators have shown a rapid adoption of newly disclosed vulnerabilities, sometimes exploiting them within days of publication. The botnet's evolution includes a shift from a shotgun approach using numerous exploits to a more focused strategy targeting recent, critical vulnerabilities. The malware shares similarities with Mirai but focuses solely on DoS attacks. This threat highlights the importance of exposure management in cybersecurity.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-04-10T15:04:08.786000","created":"2026-03-11T15:49:33.319000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"RondoDox","indicators":[{"id":3778336188,"indicator":"CVE-2023-46604","type":"CVE","created":"2026-03-11T15:49:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4085493295,"indicator":"CVE-2025-20281","type":"CVE","created":"2026-03-11T15:49:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4076977853,"indicator":"CVE-2025-24016","type":"CVE","created":"2026-03-11T15:49:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4144539394,"indicator":"CVE-2025-24893","type":"CVE","created":"2026-03-11T15:49:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4068322670,"indicator":"CVE-2025-32756","type":"CVE","created":"2026-03-11T15:49:34","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4175877408,"